WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.605
- Hey, guys, it's Michelle.

00:00:01.605 --> 00:00:02.929
If you're anything like me,

00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:04.559
you probably have a hard time

00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:06.162
stepping away from life and work

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:07.619
to focus on yourself.

00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:09.668
Today, I hope that you take five minutes

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:10.887
and do just that.

00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:13.236
This routine is great
for after a stressful day

00:00:13.236 --> 00:00:14.620
at work or studying.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.260
Today we're going to target
the lower back and hips,

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.199
which hold a lot of tension
when we're under mental stress.

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:21.813
If you want to hold any of the poses

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.235
for a little bit longer,

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:24.611
feel free to hit pause

00:00:24.611 --> 00:00:26.919
to sink into the pose
a little bit further,

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:28.970
as I'm only demoing each move,

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.516
rather than doing a full on routine.

00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:34.137
I usually like to hold each
pose for about 60 seconds

00:00:34.137 --> 00:00:35.762
to get a full muscular release,

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:37.438
but it's up to you and your body

00:00:37.438 --> 00:00:39.236
to decide what's best for you

00:00:39.236 --> 00:00:41.566
and what you need on this stressful day.

00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:44.291
So here are some great
stretches to de-stress

00:00:44.291 --> 00:00:46.010
after a long day.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.374
For the neck stretch,

00:00:47.374 --> 00:00:48.802
real your hand over your head

00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:51.697
and pull your ear towards your shoulder.

00:00:51.697 --> 00:00:53.086
You can reach your other hand

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.870
out towards the ground
for a deeper stretch.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.448
Sphinx elongates your lower back,

00:00:58.448 --> 00:01:00.232
where you'll feel a lot of tension

00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:03.243
if you drive a car or sit in a desk chair

00:01:03.243 --> 00:01:05.048
for long periods of time

00:01:05.048 --> 00:01:07.747
Sphinx transitions
really nicely into seal,

00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:09.729
another lower back stretch that also

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:11.896
elongates your abdominals.

00:01:14.652 --> 00:01:15.874
Pigeon is a tough stretch

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:17.664
to get out the kinks in your hips,

00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:20.027
which hold a lot of tension under stress.

00:01:20.027 --> 00:01:23.527
(gentle electronic music)

00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:29.243
Lizard, like pigeon,

00:01:29.243 --> 00:01:33.410
stretches out the sides of
your hips and hip flexors.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.992
Side straddle is a little
bit of an advanced pose,

00:01:41.992 --> 00:01:43.616
but I encourage you to try it out

00:01:43.616 --> 00:01:46.833
because it opens your
inner groin and side body,

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:48.372
which honestly just feels really good

00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:49.937
after a long day.

00:01:49.937 --> 00:01:52.105
Butterfly is a great stretch
for the inner thighs,

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:53.717
groin, and knees,

00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:55.495
and removes fatigue from long hours

00:01:55.495 --> 00:01:56.934
of standing and walking.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.122
If you hold the pose long enough,

00:01:58.122 --> 00:02:01.286
you'll also start to feel
it in your lower back.

00:02:01.286 --> 00:02:03.549
Lastly, child's pose is a calming

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:07.113
and surrendering pose to tie
up your stretches to de-stress.

00:02:07.113 --> 00:02:08.933
Thank you guys so much
for watching this video

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:10.592
and for trying out this routine.

00:02:10.592 --> 00:02:11.533
If you enjoyed it,

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:12.537
please give it a thumbs up,

00:02:12.537 --> 00:02:13.815
and comment below with what workout

00:02:13.815 --> 00:02:15.249
you want to see next.

00:02:15.249 --> 00:02:17.344
I hope that you feel a
little bit less stressed

00:02:17.344 --> 00:02:19.521
and ready to take on your day.

00:02:19.521 --> 00:02:20.600
Bye.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.100
(gentle electronic music)

